## ChangeLog of SoftEther VPN

## Apple Silicon (ARM64) Support - January 2026

### Added

- **Native Apple Silicon Support**: SoftEther VPN now builds natively on Apple Silicon Macs (M1, M2, M3, M4 and future processors)
- **All Core Components with ARM64 Support**:
  - ✅ VPN Server (native ARM64)
  - ✅ VPN Client (native ARM64)
  - ✅ VPN Bridge (native ARM64)
  - ✅ vpncmd Command-Line Admin Utility (native ARM64)
- **Comprehensive Documentation**:
  - `BUILD_MACOS_ARM64.md` - Detailed build instructions for Apple Silicon
  - `COMPONENTS_ARM64_SUPPORT.md` - Complete component compatibility matrix and usage guide
  - `QUICKSTART_APPLE_SILICON.md` - Quick start guide for fast setup
  - `APPLE_SILICON_SUMMARY.md` - Technical implementation details
- **Automated Setup Script**: New `setup_apple_silicon.sh` script for one-command installation
- **Architecture Detection**: Enhanced configure script to automatically detect and optimize for ARM64
- **Homebrew Integration**: Automatic detection of Homebrew library paths for both Apple Silicon and Intel Macs

### Changed

- **Configure Script**: Improved ARM64/aarch64 detection with visual feedback
- **Makefile Optimization**: Updated `macos_64bit_nobits.mak` with:
  - Native ARM64 compiler flags (`-arch arm64`)
  - Dynamic Homebrew path detection
  - Automatic OpenSSL and readline library path resolution
  - Support for `/opt/homebrew` (Apple Silicon) and `/usr/local` (Intel)
- **README**: Updated to mention Apple Silicon support and build instructions

### Technical Details

- ARM64 binaries are compiled with `-arch arm64` flag for native execution
- No Rosetta 2 translation required - true native ARM64 execution
- Optimized for performance and power efficiency on Apple Silicon
- Full compatibility with macOS 11.0 (Big Sur) and later

### Files Modified

- `configure`: Enhanced ARM64 detection and user feedback
- `src/configure`: Updated with Apple Silicon information
- `src/makefiles/macos_64bit_nobits.mak`: Complete rewrite for ARM64 optimization
- `README`: Added Apple Silicon references

### Files Created

- `BUILD_MACOS_ARM64.md`: Comprehensive build guide (NEW)
- `COMPONENTS_ARM64_SUPPORT.md`: Component compatibility matrix and detailed usage (NEW)
- `QUICKSTART_APPLE_SILICON.md`: Fast setup guide (NEW)
- `APPLE_SILICON_SUMMARY.md`: Technical implementation summary (NEW)
- `setup_apple_silicon.sh`: Automated installation script (NEW)

### Benefits for Apple Silicon Users

- ✅ Native ARM64 execution (no emulation overhead)
- ✅ Better performance compared to Rosetta 2
- ✅ Lower power consumption
- ✅ Improved thermal characteristics
- ✅ Full hardware acceleration support
- ✅ Easy setup with automated script

### Usage

For Apple Silicon Mac users:

```bash
./setup_apple_silicon.sh
```

Or manually:

```bash
./configure
make
```

For more details, see BUILD_MACOS_ARM64.md

